o, we set $x=0$ and solve the resulting equation for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =-5(0-10) \\\\ {y}^{2} & =50 \\\\ y & =\\pm \\sqrt{50} \\\\ y & =\\pm 5\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parabola intersects the $y$-axis at $(0,5\\sqrt{2})$ and $(0,-5\\sqrt{2}).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-73767/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ddc6c4b1-b4c4-52f8-9f25-feda3130e358"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73767"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-79253/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "c4c91fb6-e219-5401-9b29-aafdd6b2514c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79253/selection/968b78a1da72ee3df196b4b60a1cb9afd2082e522352c24e5babcf63ab6a5c7b" :answer/id #uuid "0eb02928-44ea-5d32-8758-0669151e9f23" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79253/selection/07791849728418b50d59d705e3d959e93383e408886fd319ae3a513a1b7159ba" :answer/id #uuid "ce6dd8fc-afbf-57c9-8fab-c8122240ba64" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79253/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "75fbc113-a573-54ec-8e74-b8ca43f3455b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79253/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "69280b0f-a6e1-548b-b3d8-14fb06c58c03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79253/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "92de9ed0-23fb-5ce3-a28d-bbdad3bb8222" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79253/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-79253/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-79253/selection/968b78a1da72ee3df196b4b60a1cb9afd2082e522352c24e5babcf63ab6a5c7b" "q-79253/selection/07791849728418b50d59d705e3d959e93383e408886fd319ae3a513a1b7159ba" "q-79253/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-79253/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79253" :question/id #uuid "55a39868-2114-5c28-aa42-9882eb80ca08" :question/math-academy-id "q-79253" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13955472/assets/32d2ecb4cc0fe71888d4ca89f0c5c493d0746ae9f97a9253ef42d69f45880086.png)\n\nWhat is the $x$-intercept of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(9,4)$ and passes through the point $(-7,12).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola with vertex $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(y-k)^{2}=4p(x-h).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $(h,k)=(9,4)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n(y-4)^{2}=4p(x-9).\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(-7,12),$ we substitute $x=-7$ and $y=12$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(12-4)^{2} & =4p(-7-9) \\\\ 64 & =4p\\cdot (-16) \\\\ p & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-4)^{2} & =-4(x-9).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $x$-axis, we must have $y=0.$ So, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve the resulting equation for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0-4)^{2} & =-4(x-9) \\\\ 16 & =-4(x-9) \\\\ -4 & =x-9 \\\\ x & =-4+9 \\\\ x & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercept is $5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-79253/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8c990d69-54da-5541-948f-0d5eff96feb5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79253"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-251784/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer/id #uuid "946e9495-5411-5a32-9d15-55fc79e6d96c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-251784/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "0c88c2c7-dac5-5150-a9a6-58bac57745c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-251784/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "a9c809e1-762d-5da3-930e-0f0f033735d7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-251784/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer-field/choices ["q-251784/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" "q-251784/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-251784/field-2/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "2a7abc9f-2db1-5402-8d85-39f7687436e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-251784/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "c38e5073-3a93-5058-ae96-d40f2f5e2a0a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-251784/field-2/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-251784/field-2/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-251784" :question/id #uuid "1cc0f48b-955c-5fb4-87fd-77527333645f" :question/math-academy-id "q-251784" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13955472/assets/afb7abacdffafd634165fd1f35868878b2bc420df6a173b48f6a17c7638f7dec.png)\n\n**From left to right**, the **exact values** of the $x$-intercepts of the parabola shown above are{{field-1}}\nand \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(-3,4)$ and passes through the point $(0,-5).$\n\nThe general standard equation of an up- or down-opening parabola with vertex $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $(h,k)=(-3,4)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+3)^{2} & =4p(y-4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(0,-5),$ we substitute $x=0$ and $y=-5$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0+3)^{2} & =4p(-5-4) \\\\ 9 & =4p(-9) \\\\ p & =-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+3)^{2} & =-(y-4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $x$-axis, we must have $y=0.$ So, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+3)^{2} & =-(0-4) \\\\ (x+3)^{2} & =4 \\\\ x+3 & =\\pm \\sqrt{4} \\\\ x & =\\pm 2-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the $x$-intercepts are $-5$  and $-1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-251784/field-1" "q-251784/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8c990d69-54da-5541-948f-0d5eff96feb5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-251784"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-240666/field-1/34d6a116cfea25ad11008d41d6152ee565691a4dc671039515875488f5520d96" :answer/id #uuid "27e7a0d0-07af-5e4e-b493-9c279e82c57b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-240666/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "dd19f6a9-87d8-507c-90b8-34b2f77c5a4a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-240666/field-1/34d6a116cfea25ad11008d41d6152ee565691a4dc671039515875488f5520d96" :answer-field/choices ["q-240666/field-1/34d6a116cfea25ad11008d41d6152ee565691a4dc671039515875488f5520d96"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-240666" :question/id #uuid "295ec8a5-8065-5b04-8ad1-001208416bc9" :question/math-academy-id "q-240666" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13955472/assets/d4c21d6ce09ff32004a28d18d223fef7858c377bccb0eb532cf2dda29a545f5e.png)\n\nThe value of the $x$-intercept of the parabola shown above is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(-7,-2)$ and passes through the point $(-11,-6).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola with vertex $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(y-k)^{2}=4p(x-h).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $(h,k)=(-7,-2)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n(y+2)^{2}=4p(x+7).\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(-11,-6),$ we substitute $x=-11$ and $y=-6$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-6+2)^{2} & =4p(-11+7) \\\\ (-4)^{2} & =4p\\cdot (-4) \\\\ 16 & =-16p \\\\ p & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+2)^{2} & =-4(x+7).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $x$-axis, we must have $y=0.$ So, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0+2)^{2} & =-4(x+7) \\\\ 4 & =-4(x+7) \\\\ -1 & =x+7 \\\\ x & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercept is $-8.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-240666/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8c990d69-54da-5541-948f-0d5eff96feb5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-240666"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73832/selection/9d24149fae7ed3c8ded173362d1185a392e9450a68167efe583749113804f5b7" :answer/id #uuid "67e04df4-c99e-5b38-b2a3-89274f048a3f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0$ and $4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73832/selection/c1e3cf842487182bde7753bba47457411a61c70c7a268a54a2a4e937e47261fe" :answer/id #uuid "73029ed4-5320-5eec-a240-5c35a9fd06e1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0$ and $2\\sqrt{5}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73832/selection/28fd85fa4c8cc89e80bb170d854720a0f401634897152ebf4cbef0e7aac2f1ef" :answer/id #uuid "ffb61613-6a7a-569d-ae98-a4dc317ebffc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0$  and $\\sqrt{5}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73832/selection/5fa4c39b15cc0ffb8b6d7c3b0aa2e8c8b8211499ea9b915f73a618ae3fe2bf04" :answer/id #uuid "cadabb28-2da1-5b93-8bc9-22ee579109d5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0$ and $3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73832/selection/3fcbca23588d2cfc9bf6d7f093dc7d25092ec606dbd229a842d09d1c0725af85" :answer/id #uuid "10927cd1-a48a-5c2c-baac-cf2d39d3711b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$0$ and $5$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73832/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7aae2332-ed70-5fef-961b-4db1af133793" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73832/selection/9d24149fae7ed3c8ded173362d1185a392e9450a68167efe583749113804f5b7" :answer-field/choices ["q-73832/selection/9d24149fae7ed3c8ded173362d1185a392e9450a68167efe583749113804f5b7" "q-73832/selection/c1e3cf842487182bde7753bba47457411a61c70c7a268a54a2a4e937e47261fe" "q-73832/selection/28fd85fa4c8cc89e80bb170d854720a0f401634897152ebf4cbef0e7aac2f1ef" "q-73832/selection/5fa4c39b15cc0ffb8b6d7c3b0aa2e8c8b8211499ea9b915f73a618ae3fe2bf04" "q-73832/selection/3fcbca23588d2cfc9bf6d7f093dc7d25092ec606dbd229a842d09d1c0725af85"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73832" :question/id #uuid "166cdda3-01a4-5828-9800-429450a46515" :question/math-academy-id "q-73832" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13955472/assets/e79a3a7c2fce5a3e3ec7d838ebe1327dcc5452168f499fad05eea85a08e8f8b0.png)\n\nWhat are the $x$-intercepts of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(2,-1)$ and passes through the point $(-2,3).$\n\nThe general standard equation of an up- or down-opening parabola with vertex $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $(h,k)=(2,-1)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2} & =4p(y+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(-2,3),$ we substitute $x=-2$ and $y=3$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2-2)^{2} & =4p(3+1) \\\\ 16 & =4p(4) \\\\ p & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2} & =4(y+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $x$-axis, we must have $y=0.$ So, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2} & =4(0+1) \\\\ (x-2)^{2} & =4 \\\\ x-2 & =\\pm \\sqrt{4} \\\\ x & =\\pm 2+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercepts are $0$ and $4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-73832/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8c990d69-54da-5541-948f-0d5eff96feb5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73832"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-251699/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer/id #uuid "8e655a02-fa82-562a-8cb5-966692875652" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-251699/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f0ed16da-cc28-5863-9b17-bcd8a2c0b6df" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-251699/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer-field/choices ["q-251699/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-251699/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "eb8eca46-9fc7-5f1e-89e5-fa5942c1ab85" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-251699/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "ef1585fd-d627-5dcf-91f7-8cbfb940c537" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-251699/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-251699/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-251699" :question/id #uuid "d5d338c0-23c4-51e8-bf62-58aee9a4f5b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-251699" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13955472/assets/0da514f806c56689fdf4be724223e75c42559aa16ae38470bf088a83d299aaa9.png)\n\n**From left to right**, the values of the $x$-intercepts of the parabola shown above are{{field-1}}\nand \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(-1,-8)$ and passes through the point $(5,10).$\n\nThe general standard equation of an up- or down-opening parabola with vertex $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $(h,k)=(-1,-8)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)^{2} & =4p(y+8).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(5,10),$ we substitute $x=5$ and $y=10$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(5+1)^{2} & =4p(10+8) \\\\ 36 & =4p(18) \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)^{2} & =2(y+8).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $x$-axis, we must have $y=0.$ So, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)^{2} & =2(0+8) \\\\ (x+1)^{2} & =16 \\\\ x+1 & =\\pm \\sqrt{16} \\\\ x & =\\pm 4-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the $x$-intercepts are $-5$  and $3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-251699/field-1" "q-251699/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8c990d69-54da-5541-948f-0d5eff96feb5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-251699"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-79294/selection/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" :answer/id #uuid "e8dd48bc-6287-5249-811e-1ba720cc2d33" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79294/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "826d45e3-678e-5285-a460-50fd437102d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79294/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "d208579a-7d47-5372-9e40-973c3b6d6d1c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79294/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "525ee57b-bc73-5071-9967-ea4c8586aed4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79294/selection/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" :answer/id #uuid "3a7ced0b-c506-5165-8809-3ef8ab3b5fe7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79294/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "62e7e25d-6239-522b-9cfa-1980d98e984f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79294/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer-field/choices ["q-79294/selection/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" "q-79294/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" "q-79294/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" "q-79294/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" "q-79294/selection/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79294" :question/id #uuid "3caa4df9-5e0c-5ecf-8e43-c8fb646eb03c" :question/math-academy-id "q-79294" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13955472/assets/407f89e40691ddaefd912c97dc9e8b15a08e0120ad2cf1c9a277417cd8380e98.png)\n\nWhat is the $y$-intercept of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(4,-4)$ and passes through the point $(7,5).$\n\nThe general standard equation of an up- or down-opening parabola with vertex at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k),\n$$\n\nand substituting $(h,k)=(4,-4)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n(x-4)^{2}=4p(y+4).\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(7,5),$ we substitute $x=7$ and $y=5$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(7-4)^{2} & =4p(5+4) \\\\ 9 & =4p(9) \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-4)^{2} & =y+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $y$-axis, we must have $x=0.$ So, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0-4)^{2} & =y+4 \\\\ 16 & =y+4 \\\\ y & =16-4 \\\\ y & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercept is $12.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-79294/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e182f71-db24-5c29-9c8b-2fc4b5ab5dd8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79294"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-165434/selection/819a757d4e0bc485722090a78c1e2f2785f28af835c17515ba5670f2d7cae63c" :answer/id #uuid "5e8b9bd4-fac1-5905-a346-2c5785dccf75" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-2$ and $4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165434/selection/7723f1eebc074448fc359e9bfa8644efe89ff6a0b4d43df92838c4e699c1926c" :answer/id #uuid "39b2902f-7269-55ed-b64d-21a49e01c410" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-1$ and $3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165434/selection/35281f68742a3d8bfaf78f7c3816f7e2a40e47f7b4070c91699ee06852e46952" :answer/id #uuid "eac601b7-b428-57ab-a182-f986c1ddc836" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-\\frac{1}{2}$ and $3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165434/selection/a304f7c7f8a4c6ff9ac349ee42c59819aa98d58679d84bb1afe66aa4ace41878" :answer/id #uuid "0d286ef6-36b7-521a-8fe1-d87f2694928a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-1$ and $4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165434/selection/acd637ff1b61e70ac202d4593059b2d0e737a61f1786eb55a8ef23393f048a65" :answer/id #uuid "c61de2ee-64f4-588a-b4d3-0aebd6c40656" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-\\frac{1}{2}$ and $2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165434/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "86262259-005d-57ec-85bf-24880b46069d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-165434/selection/819a757d4e0bc485722090a78c1e2f2785f28af835c17515ba5670f2d7cae63c" :answer-field/choices ["q-165434/selection/819a757d4e0bc485722090a78c1e2f2785f28af835c17515ba5670f2d7cae63c" "q-165434/selection/7723f1eebc074448fc359e9bfa8644efe89ff6a0b4d43df92838c4e699c1926c" "q-165434/selection/35281f68742a3d8bfaf78f7c3816f7e2a40e47f7b4070c91699ee06852e46952" "q-165434/selection/a304f7c7f8a4c6ff9ac349ee42c59819aa98d58679d84bb1afe66aa4ace41878" "q-165434/selection/acd637ff1b61e70ac202d4593059b2d0e737a61f1786eb55a8ef23393f048a65"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-165434" :question/id #uuid "20250ecc-bc9a-594d-a7f9-8fe791acfa2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-165434" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13955472/assets/6450376de8f9f4c0c8f5b414d95de67839664eda4f2056376160caddef47ba1f.png)\n\nWhat are the $y$-intercepts of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(\\frac{9}{2},1)$ and passes through the point $(4,0).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola with vertex at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(y-k)^{2}=4p(x-h),\n$$\n\nand substituting $(h,k)=(\\frac{9}{2},1)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n(y-1)^{2}=4p(x-\\frac{9}{2}).\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(4,0),$ we substitute $x=4$ and $y=0$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0-1)^{2} & =4p(4-\\frac{9}{2}) \\\\ 1 & =4p(-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\ p & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-1)^{2}=-2(x-\\frac{9}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $y$-axis, we must have $x=0.$ So, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-1)^{2} & =(0+9) \\\\ (y-1)^{2} & =9 \\\\ y-1 & =\\pm 3 \\\\ y & =-2,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercepts are $-2$ and $4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-165434/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e182f71-db24-5c29-9c8b-2fc4b5ab5dd8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-165434"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-165433/selection/5d022a88a643e97abec4d01dfce48411101475c0705a98f29f3a8e3560fb0616" :answer/id #uuid "7ce16ccf-bf1a-5e0f-95f0-a49070129e73" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165433/selection/c54a7015f3c3f367ecf5b4ccb4da0cb7bd0a129bea7820ab05f4f7a142cba09f" :answer/id #uuid "23c483bf-8201-5984-8008-743dbbcb908d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\sqrt{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165433/selection/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45" :answer/id #uuid "bebf9dd7-d488-5833-8a26-6291e0a0e012" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165433/selection/10293ac0295e0e79554137a949f5c5c46b9812dcc0a3ecb6349c4cb5e6acdff3" :answer/id #uuid "ab0feba6-4ed8-5c50-aba8-7a6a1ba9b689" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165433/selection/e6750dfeef469bc6659a87c7aa39e93316647bb3f61898710c295df660d50249" :answer/id #uuid "fafa2fe9-c298-54ae-9840-3a425a91e6d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\sqrt{20}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165433/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1e088981-d698-536c-8dbb-b27115580bc5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-165433/selection/5d022a88a643e97abec4d01dfce48411101475c0705a98f29f3a8e3560fb0616" :answer-field/choices ["q-165433/selection/5d022a88a643e97abec4d01dfce48411101475c0705a98f29f3a8e3560fb0616" "q-165433/selection/c54a7015f3c3f367ecf5b4ccb4da0cb7bd0a129bea7820ab05f4f7a142cba09f" "q-165433/selection/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45" "q-165433/selection/10293ac0295e0e79554137a949f5c5c46b9812dcc0a3ecb6349c4cb5e6acdff3" "q-165433/selection/e6750dfeef469bc6659a87c7aa39e93316647bb3f61898710c295df660d50249"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-165433" :question/id #uuid "d8bf318e-dc63-500a-966e-f40512cc20a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-165433" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13955472/assets/616116b9e5cf137c526b11dc5ce1647cd8f9cbd3a652be6dade9a8769467c27c.png)\n\nWhat is the $y$-intercept of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(5,15)$ and passes through the point $(2,6).$\n\nThe general standard equation of an up- or down-opening parabola with vertex at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k),\n$$\n\nand substituting $(h,k)=(5,15)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n(x-5)^{2}=4p(y-15).\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(2,6),$ we substitute $x=2$ and $y=6$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2-5)^{2} & =4p(6-15) \\\\ 9 & =4p(-9) \\\\ p & =-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-5)^{2} & =-(y-15).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $y$-axis, we must have $x=0.$ So, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0-5)^{2} & =-(y-15) \\\\ 25 & =-y+15 \\\\ y & =15-25 \\\\ y & =-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercept is $-10.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-165433/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e182f71-db24-5c29-9c8b-2fc4b5ab5dd8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-165433"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-251810/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "57c30cdc-0333-55e2-a937-59c5db3cd652" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-251810/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "342eabd8-334e-540b-a0f0-fb6d6f7a0ccb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-251810/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-251810/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-251810" :question/id #uuid "f600f675-ff18-55ea-865f-e9845a197e99" :question/math-academy-id "q-251810" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13955472/assets/31618ee78ebe4834cf76aedebce7c25eca8413c6a4b9d91761ccc38dbd32b01d.png)\n\nThe value of the $y$-intercept of the parabola shown above  is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(2,2)$ and passes through the point $(-2,-2).$\n\nThe general standard equation of an up- or down-opening parabola with vertex at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k),\n$$\n\nand substituting $(h,k)=(2,2)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n(x-2)^{2}=4p(y-2).\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(-2,-2),$ we substitute $x=-2$ and $y=-2$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2-2)^{2} & =4p(-2-2) \\\\ 16 & =4p(-4) \\\\ p & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2} & =-4(y-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $y$-axis, we must have $x=0.$ So, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0-2)^{2} & =-4(y-2) \\\\ 4 & =-4(y-2) \\\\ -1 & =y-2 \\\\ y & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercept is $1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-251810/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e182f71-db24-5c29-9c8b-2fc4b5ab5dd8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-251810"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-251799/field-1/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" :answer/id #uuid "b0a5ef85-a6ba-5f22-bbd7-e710a552ca28" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-251799/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "35ce529b-8c25-5991-9fc9-9bc09b935ddd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-251799/field-1/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" :answer-field/choices ["q-251799/field-1/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-251799" :question/id #uuid "4337d6a2-0dad-5b6f-9de4-86a4ea9d212e" :question/math-academy-id "q-251799" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13955472/assets/d589816d2368a450c0b2bbc1d3c6323b09b9d6dc5272f67a505b80f0688b16ae.png)\n\nThe value of the $y$-intercept of the parabola shown above  is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(-3,-2)$ and passes through the point $(-7,6).$\n\nThe general standard equation of an up- or down-opening parabola with vertex at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k),\n$$\n\nand substituting $(h,k)=(-3,-2)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n(x+3)^{2}=4p(y+2).\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(-7,6),$ we substitute $x=-7$ and $y=6$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-7+3)^{2} & =4p(6+2) \\\\ 16 & =4p(8) \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+3)^{2} & =2(y+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $y$-axis, we must have $x=0.$ So, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0+3)^{2} & =2(y+2) \\\\ 9 & =2(y+2) \\\\ \\frac{9}{2} & =y+2 \\\\ y & =\\frac{9}{2}-2 \\\\ y & =\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercept is $\\frac{5}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-251799/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e182f71-db24-5c29-9c8b-2fc4b5ab5dd8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-251799"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
